:"p","text":"Museums are increasingly becoming digital knowledge institutions, combining physical collections with digital archives, 3D models, GIS, virtual exhibitions, and AI-assisted discovery."},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital Museum Specialist"},{"text":"Digital Heritage Curator"},{"text":"Heritage Data Analyst"},{"text":"AI Museum Collections Specialist"},{"text":"Virtual Museum Designer"},{"text":"3D Heritage Documentation Specialist"},{"text":"Cultural Heritage Data Scientist"},{"text":"Digital Archaeology Specialist"},{"text":"Heritage GIS Analyst"},{"text":"Museum Technology Manager"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Future workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Physical Artefact","Digital Imaging / 3D Capture","Metadata","Digital Repository","Knowledge Graph","AI-Assisted Discovery","Virtual Exhibition","Global Public Access"]},{"type":"p","text":"AI can assist with metadata suggestions, image classification, search, translation, visitor personalisation, and collection discovery, but historical interpretation, provenance decisions, conservation decisions, and cultural sensitivity require qualified human oversight."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Core"},{"type":"flow","items":["Ancient Indian History","Archaeology","Art & Culture"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Museum"},{"type":"flow","items":["Museology","Collection Management","Cataloguing","Exhibition Development"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Heritage"},{"type":"flow","items":["Heritage Documentation","Conservation Awareness","Provenance Research"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"flow","items":["Digital Archives","Metadata","GIS","Photography","Photogrammetry","3D Documentation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excel","SQL","Power BI","Python"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["Historical Research","Source Criticism","Academic Writing","Citation Management"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"flow","items":["Digital Humanities","AI-Assisted Heritage Research","Knowledge Graphs","Virtual Museums"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Progression"},{"type":"h","text":"0–2 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Museum Intern","Museum Assistant","Collection/Documentation Assistant"]},{"type":"h","text":"2–5 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Collections Assistant","Curatorial Assistant","Museum Research/Documentation Specialist"]},{"type":"h","text":"5–8 years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Curator","Senior Curator","Collections Specialist/Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"8+ years"},{"type":"flow","items":["Collections Manager","Museum Manager","Museum Director / Heritage Programme Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Best overall strategy"},{"type":"p","text":"For BA Ancient Indian History, Culture & Archaeology → Museum Assistant, the strongest pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Ancient History","Archaeology","Museology","Collection Management","Digital Heritage","GIS","Research"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The BA provides the historical and archaeological foundation, while practical museum experience, object documentation, cataloguing, exhibition work, and postgraduate specialisation significantly improve progression toward curator and collections-management roles. Adding GIS, 3D documentation, digital archives, and AI-assisted heritage technologies can also position the graduate for the rapidly expanding digital-heritage sector."}]}]}